{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08G4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$E$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0004": "$E$", "MATH_0005": "$E$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-perfect}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fc5237f1b4c1ceca1670443ab7e2998bcd39b8fde93088658de09d8203488f7a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9aaaf622a4ad36e4eb3cf2f58bd5699206ca26ca90defd27e6e34b5ec933e9d2", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an object of <MATH_0003>.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is perfect, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is pseudo-coherent and locally has finite tor dimension.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c1ea36a6c7ad0f45dddf256aa1f381b857b86a9b6ee1f156adb7214cf1ff3dde", "unit_id": "tag:08G8:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08G4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$E|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0005": "$E$", "MATH_0006": "$m$", "MATH_0007": "$m$", "MATH_0008": "$E|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0011": "$U$", "MATH_0012": "$a \\leq b$", "MATH_0013": "$E|_U$", "MATH_0014": "$[a, b]$", "MATH_0015": "$E|_U$", "MATH_0016": "$m$", "MATH_0017": "$m$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pseudo-coherent-independent-representative}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-tor-amplitude}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-perfect-precise}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:96f5996a81ade13fb869e5b8a9e5b2057444644862f88972e77a44b26befe520", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ebc9c31973f8e53109df60a5cf3be7270df4a57a1813e510e033cdb37d40ed6d", "source_text": "Assume (1). Let <MATH_0001> be an object of <MATH_0002>.\nBy definition there exists a covering <MATH_0003> such that\n<MATH_0004> is represented by a strictly perfect complex.\nThus <MATH_0005> is pseudo-coherent (i.e., <MATH_0006>-pseudo-coherent for all <MATH_0007>) by\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nMoreover, a direct summand of a finite free module is flat, hence\n<MATH_0008> has finite Tor dimension by\nLemma <REF_0002>. Thus (2) holds.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume (2). Let <MATH_0009> be an object of <MATH_0010>.\nAfter replacing <MATH_0011> by the members of a covering\nwe may assume there exist integers <MATH_0012> such that <MATH_0013>\nhas tor amplitude in <MATH_0014>. Since <MATH_0015> is <MATH_0016>-pseudo-coherent\nfor all <MATH_0017> we conclude using Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:540c6dd93a8cf7aaac8a778d9b29d60678eafc0ba29ca7a2dbbe40b0103ef100", "unit_id": "tag:08G8:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08G4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(f, f^\\sharp) : (\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n(\\mathcal{D}, \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$E$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0004": "$E$", "MATH_0005": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0006": "$Lf^*E$", "MATH_0007": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-perfect-pullback}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:078f77d17419e8c5000a914b82ff9fa257d7a92b958b421a676e0b21ade125a9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7a1326e3b2080fd94f797254d6797354fb36eb859606275cd7d63f5680272cbf", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a morphism of ringed sites.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an object of <MATH_0003>.\nIf <MATH_0004> is perfect in <MATH_0005>,\nthen <MATH_0006> is perfect in <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:070f6d4fd2b83566dde61444bc4644191334ca2a570dc975864d86a550aa89a4", "unit_id": "tag:08H6:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08G4", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-perfect}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-tor-amplitude-pullback}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-pseudo-coherent-pullback}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:317ecddeed296f33cca336ee9cb8fbf58c8c8d433b9e2ff474ff0b261badeacb", "source_text": "This follows from Lemma <REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:600cf53eef358844634c10459102d9a4bb489b0cb7f33711842aae8b39a8cc23", "unit_id": "tag:08H6:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08G4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$(K, L, M, f, g, h)$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0004": "$K, L, M$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-two-out-of-three-perfect}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:076df254e083dccd98da0f46a15e288ebd3ef9c655864c52015b9b448073feb1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cb645c0354543d314a70d60da98f1bfd73fe75248b9149ad0d2386fe457ce00c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a distinguished triangle in <MATH_0003>. If two out of three of\n<MATH_0004> are perfect then the third is also perfect.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:514b2550de442a3a23fc48c68d0a420de46c59fa31738a3a7218d3c01bfa4440", "unit_id": "tag:08G9:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08G4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$K$", "MATH_0002": "$L$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$K|_U$", "MATH_0007": "$L|_U$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{L}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0010": "$U$", "MATH_0011": "$K|_U \\to L|_U$", "MATH_0012": "$\\alpha : \\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{L}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0013": "$M|_U$", "MATH_0014": "$\\alpha$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-perfect}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-cone-pseudo-coherent}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-cone-tor-amplitude}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-local-actual}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-cone}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:31bfd501ca7343ffe72ba4f0eb40d9d36d27a8119ac6c2e1bc789adec5da7062", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:567b0e5de9fd41b859adc8288bca2e1cd4a2a070728f8d716918b2ce31f80682", "source_text": "First proof: Combine\nLemmas <REF_0001>, <REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003>.\nSecond proof (sketch): Say <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are perfect. Let <MATH_0003> be an object\nof <MATH_0004>. After replacing\n<MATH_0005> by the members of a covering we may assume that <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007>\nare represented by strictly perfect complexes <MATH_0008>\nand <MATH_0009>. After replacing <MATH_0010> by the members\nof a covering we may assume the map <MATH_0011> is given by\na map of complexes <MATH_0012>,\nsee Lemma <REF_0004>.\nThen <MATH_0013> is isomorphic to the cone of <MATH_0014> which is strictly\nperfect by Lemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d380df319e28108477deea6a9c19b76835b069b4f981e6f112fb85d1b45d2235", "unit_id": "tag:08G9:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08G4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$K, L$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0004": "$K \\otimes_\\mathcal{O}^\\mathbf{L} L$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-tensor-perfect}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ba65ece5537a90eb70abd3eded69ada1b33cb3d98e8e853552ffd4c199167ef7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f9884096de98e464d2e0dfb96d019c38adfe40e97af6698708b10af737457aea", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nIf <MATH_0002> are perfect objects of <MATH_0003>, then\nso is <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f360d0075358eb6ff36f09abb46e5fb26f51715ebabe6b45eab2d2f207f0fe35", "unit_id": "tag:09JB:statement"}
